### Summary of behavior implemented

- `-f`/`--force`: sets policy to non-interactive (no prompt). Repetitions idempotent.
- `-i`/`--interactive`: sets policy to interactive (prompt when destination exists).
- Last occurrence wins: `-i -f` → no prompt; `-f -i` → prompt.
- Prompt goes to stderr, names the effective destination, reads one line from stdin.
- Affirm only when first character is `y` or `Y` (no leading whitespace tolerated). Decline on any other initial, blank line, or EOF.
- Decline leaves both source and destination unchanged, marks `any_failed = true`, and continues to next source.
- No prompt is emitted when the destination does not exist.
- All base behavior (error diagnostics, exit codes, per-source continuation) is preserved.

